Change (non-test lines only; no test is added or changed). Every hunk replaces calls that the
translation cannot handle by calls to the new private module `prim` or by loops without an
early return, and keeps the computed values:
 prim  New private module `prim` at the end of the file (before `mod tests`): twelve one-line
       wrappers, opaque in the translation and modelled in Lean, each the original expression:
       sha256 (`Sha256::digest(bytes).into()`), find_query_or_fragment (`s.find(['?', '#'])`),
       strip_suffix / strip_prefix (`&str` patterns), last_slash_segment
       (`s.rsplit('/').next().unwrap_or(s)`), split_slash / split_percent
       (`s.split(c).map(str::to_owned).collect()`), join_slash (`segments.join("/")`),
       split_once_percent (`s.split_once('%')`), percent_encode_controls
       (`utf8_percent_encode(value, CONTROLS).into()`), percent_decode_utf8
       (`percent_decode_str(s).decode_utf8().ok().map(Cow::into_owned)`), nfkc
       (`s.nfkc().collect()`). Used by H1-H7.
 H1  sha256_digest: `prim::sha256` instead of `Sha256::digest`; the hex digits are pushed with
     the new private helper `lower_hex_digit` instead of `write!(digest, "{byte:02x}")`.
 H2  Skill::validate: the name check through `prim::percent_decode_utf8` and `prim::nfkc`
     (a `match`); the `any` over the files and the `for` loop with early returns become `while`
     loops that `break`, the latter storing the error in `result`, which is returned after the
     loop.
 H3  skill_name_from_uri: `prim::find_query_or_fragment`, `prim::strip_suffix` (twice) and
     `prim::last_slash_segment` instead of `contains`, `strip_suffix` and `rsplit`.
 H4  is_valid_skill_name: the NFKC characters collected by `prim::nfkc` and read with an index
     loop instead of `for (index, ch) in name.nfkc().enumerate()`.
 H5  manifest_resource_key: `prim::strip_suffix`, `prim::strip_prefix`,
     `prim::find_query_or_fragment`, `prim::split_slash` and `prim::join_slash`; the last segment
     taken with `Vec::pop` instead of `Split::next_back`; the dot-segment loop moved to the new
     private helpers `resolve_segments` and `resolve_segment` (no early return in a loop; the
     resolved segments are `String`s).
 H6  normalize_percent_encoding: `prim::percent_encode_controls`, `prim::split_once_percent`
     and `prim::split_percent`; the loop body moved verbatim to the new private helper
     `push_normalized_part`, with `hex.bytes().all(..)` as the new helper `is_ascii_hex` (an
     index loop) and the unreserved test as the new helper `is_unreserved`.
 H7  is_sha256_digest: `prim::strip_prefix` instead of `str::strip_prefix`.
 H8  validate_skills: the set key is `normalize_percent_encoding(&skill.uri).into_owned()`
     (a `String`) instead of the `Cow<str>`.
 H9  SkillResource::verify: `if digest == self.digest { return Ok(()); } Err(..)` instead of
     `if digest != self.digest { return Err(..); } Ok(())`.

Why each hunk is needed (each measured alone on 2026-11-25: the patched file with that one
function reverted to the original, everything else, including the Charon settings and the
script above, as in the repository):
 H1  Charon reports errors ("GATs cannot work with the `--lift-associated-types` option")
     on hybrid-array's `ArraySize` and `impl IntoIterator for Array` (skill.rs lines 121 and
     124 of that file: `Sha256::digest`, `for byte in hash`), and the script stops.
 H2  "[Error] Early returns inside of loops are not supported yet" on Skill::validate; Aeneas
     ignores its body and exits with 1.
 H3  "[Error] Unimplemented": the signatures of `str::strip_suffix`, `str::rsplit` and
     `RSplit::next` (the `core::str::pattern::Pattern` trait, `core/src/str/pattern.rs` line
     99, has a generic associated type) cannot be translated; Aeneas fails (CFailure).
 H4  Not needed for the translation: without it everything translates. It is kept (human
     decision 2026-11-25) because without it the translation calls
     `<&str as UnicodeNormalization>::nfkc` and `<Recompositions<Chars> as Iterator>::next`
     and needs the external type `unicode_normalization::recompose::Recompositions`, a stateful
     streaming iterator; with H4, NFKC is reached only through `prim::nfkc`, one function from a
     string to its characters, modelled by the opaque `ExtModel.nfkc` shared with H2.
 H5  "[Error] Unimplemented": the signatures of `str::strip_suffix` and of
     `DoubleEndedIterator::next_back` for `str::Split` (the `Pattern` trait); Aeneas fails.
 H6  "[Error] Unimplemented" on the `Pattern` trait (pattern.rs line 99) through
     `split_once('%')` and `split('%')`; Aeneas fails (exit 2).
 H7  "[Error] Unimplemented" on the `Pattern` trait through `str::strip_prefix`; Aeneas fails
     (exit 2).
 H8  "[Error] Unimplemented: found a loan and its corresponding borrow in the same region
     abstraction" on validate_skills (the `HashSet<Cow<'_, str>>` borrowing each `skill.uri`
     across iterations); Aeneas exits with 1.
 H9  Not needed for the translation: without it everything translates. It is kept (human
     decision 2026-11-25) because `!=` on `String` makes Aeneas require the `ne` method of the
     external `PartialEq` impls, adding three externals (`ne` of `char`, of `String` against
     `str` and of `Arc<T>`) that no target otherwise needs.
No upstream Charon or Aeneas issue has been filed (as of 2026-11-25); the variants are kept
outside the repository.
With the whole patch all twenty targets K01-K20 and the private helpers is_valid_skill_name,
manifest_resource_key and normalize_percent_encoding translate with real bodies, no sorry is
generated, and every earlier block of Funs.lean and Types.lean is unchanged up to its Source
